 "observations": [
  "The page number «125» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the right the number of the table, «Tab. 14», in bold sans serif, underlined. The titles (L01, L02), in bold, the sigla and the note number in roman: L01 that of C and O, L02 that of N; the folios of the manuscripts, «C 50v, O 107r,» over «N 15r.», stand at the left of the titles, the letters raised; here as left margin notes. The page has no signature.",
  "The table: a thick and a thin rule above the head, a double rule below it; vertical rules divide the fifteen columns, double ones before and after each column of arguments; thin rules under the heads that span the four columns of signs, degrees, minutes and seconds, whose heads «Sig.», «Gr.», «Min.», «Sec.» are set in small bold type, only the first «Min.» and «Sec.» with note numbers. «Numerus dierum», «Numerus horarum» and «Partes3) horarum» are printed turned through a quarter, reading upwards, in two lines; here their words stand in L03 and L04. Each printed row is one line here, the cells separated by our «|»; a head followed by empty cells spans their columns. The hours end with 24 (L29).",
  "L06-L35. Checked against the daily mean motion of Mars of Tab. 13 (p. 124, JP2 0156), 31′ 26.47″ with Brahmagupta's parameter: the days agree with n × 31′ 26.47″ to within 0.8″ (with the readings of notes a and b), except the 28 days, printed 14° 40′ 51″, computed 14° 40′ 21.1″: the seconds are 30 too large, between 14° 8′ 54″ and 15° 11′ 47″ of the 27 and 29 days, which step by 31′ 26″ and 31′ 27″ through the computed value; no note bears on them. The hours agree with n × 1′ 18.6″ to within 0.7″ (with the readings of notes c-g), and the «partes horarum», the sixtieths of an hour, with 1.31″ to the part to within 1″, some values rounded and some cut off (with the readings of notes h and i).",
  "L22, the 17 hours, printed 0s 9° 22′ 16″: see the critical note. N02: «V. notas in tab. 8.», in italics; N04: «corr. ex.», in italics."
